  m_Name: packet-loss
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: GameTerms.Runtime::GameTerms.GlossaryTermAsset
  data:
    Id: packet-loss
    Term: Packet Loss
    Abbreviation: 
    Category: 5
    Difficulty: 1
    ShortDefinition: Network packets that never arrive and must be recovered or tolerated
      by the game.
    SimpleExplanation: Some messages vanish on the way and never show up.
    WhyItMatters: Games must stay playable even when the network drops data.
    Example: A lost input packet is resent or reconstructed from later state.
    CommonMistake: Assuming a perfect network during design and playtesting only
      on LAN.
    PracticePrompt: Simulate 5 percent packet loss and list which systems break first.
    GameUses:
    - Mobile networks
    - Competitive play
    - Netcode QA
    RelatedTermIds:
    - jitter
    - latency
    - rollback
    Tags:
    - networking
    - reliability
    - qa
    Synonyms: []
    CodeExample: 
    HasDiagram: 0
    DiagramType: 0
